0065 - dw_mmc: polled completion for small reads (poll_bytes / poll_ns),
       default ON at 16 KiB; hardware CMD12 (auto_stop) priced and NOT built
=========================================================================

Full copy of drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c from linux-71-port (it includes 0012,
0014, 0039, 0063 and 0064's sdtrace). No dw_mmc.h, dw_mmc-pltfm.c, block.c
or defconfig change. Apply by copying over the port tree's file, then
`./docker/build.sh 'cd /src && $S31_MAKE linux'`, `make sync-images &&
make flash-linux`, confirm with `uname -a` (#377 or later), and grep the
build log case-insensitively for `warning:` - the only two in dw_mmc.c
(`dw_mci_ns_worst` / `dw_mci_ns_total` unused) predate 0039 and are not new.

Companions: rootfs/sdlat.c gained a BYTES form (`512b`, `1024b`; `4`, `4k`,
`1m` unchanged; the report prints `512B`) and rootfs/build-sdlat.sh builds
it in the container; board/ holds the A/B scripts, each with its runsh
timeout and its pass/kill rule in the header. The working copies live in
artifacts/tracks/polled/.

STATUS: SHIPPED 2026-09-24, kernel #377 (poll_bytes=16384 default). The
knob stays runtime: `echo 0 > /sys/module/dw_mmc/parameters/poll_bytes`
is the old kernel, no rebuild.

WHAT IT DOES

Kernel #373 (0063 mode 2 + sdtrace) completes a 4 KiB swap-in in the
host's BH and hands the faulter one wake-up. With the `none` scheduler the
faulting task IS the issuing task (blk_finish_plug -> blk_mq_flush_plug_list
issues directly; mmc's queue is BLK_MQ_F_BLOCKING; dw_mci_request() runs in
the faulter under spin_lock_bh - 02-preflight confirms: sdlat pinned to
CPU0 min 1.00 / p50 1.50 with 1.9 ctxt per request, to CPU1 1.19 / 1.31
with 2.6). So after dw_mci_start_request() the driver drops host->lock with
spin_unlock() - NOT _bh, the same split dw_mci_request_end() uses - and
dw_mci_poll_request() spins for up to poll_ns: read MINTSTS / IDSTS&IDINTEN,
call dw_mci_interrupt() when set (legal from non-IRQ context, the lost-irq
hrtimer already does), and run dw_mci_work_func() inline whenever
pending_events is non-zero. With the DONE_COMPLETE cap the request
completes inside that inline work_func: mmc_request_done ->
mmc_blk_mq_req_done -> blk_mq_complete_request -> blk_mq_raise_softirq, and
raise_softirq_irqoff() does not wake ksoftirqd because BH-disabled counts
as in_interrupt(). The BLOCK_SOFTIRQ then drains at dw_mci_request()'s
spin_unlock_bh, in the faulter, before do_swap_page reaches
folio_lock_or_retry: the folio is already unlocked, no sleep, no wake-up,
no VM_FAULT_RETRY second walk.

Gates: reads only, in_task() and IRQs enabled, no sbc, the cap set for this
request (mode 2 sets it per read; mode 0 never polls), data <= poll_bytes.
Every queue_work(system_bh_wq) site is untouched, so a redundant bh_work
runs at the unlock (finds STATE_IDLE, no events, one same-CPU dispatch, no
switch) and budget expiry can never lose a completion - that safety net is
what turned the bug below into a tail instead of a hang.

sdprobe gained `poll n/hit/expired/avg_ns`.

THE BUG THE FIRST CUT HAD (kernel #374, fixed in #375)

The loop ran work_func only when pending_events CHANGED since the last
pass, with the `seen` snapshot taken AFTER the pass. When the card answered
fast (c2d ~100 us) the DTO/XFER hardirq landed inside the CMD_COMPLETE pass
after its XFER check, so the new DATA|XFER bits equalled `seen` and the
loop spun until the budget expired. Visible three ways: p90 tracked the
budget (poll_ns 500000 -> 1.8-2.1 ms, 1500000 -> 2.5, 3000000 -> 4.06-4.10
= budget + 1.1 ms); expired 17-27% of reads pinned to CPU0 vs 0.3% on
CPU1 (there the real BH on CPU0 rescued them); and the sdtrace ring rows
read c2d 86-110 / x2bh 2984-3013 / nbh 3. Fix: call work_func whenever
pending_events is non-zero (idempotent under host->lock; a bit that cannot
be consumed yet - DATA_COMPLETE before XFER_COMPLETE, d2x 7-31 us - costs
one lock/unlock per iteration until it can). On #375 expired is 1-2 of 300
at 1.5 ms (the card's genuine tail) and p90 no longer follows the budget.

A2 / B3: HARDWARE CMD12 PRICED AND KILLED (no build)

sdlat bytes form, kernel #373, 3 rounds x 300 random, idle desktop:
    512 B  = CMD17 alone       cmds_all 1/req, last_opcode 17, ~1.8 IRQ/req
             min 0.929 / 0.929 / 0.932   p50 1.233 / 1.246 / 1.100 ms
    1024 B = CMD18 + sw CMD12  cmds_all 2/req, last_opcode 12, ~2.8 IRQ/req
             min 0.999 / 1.061 / 1.027   p50 1.282 / 1.285 / 1.295 ms
    stop_leg = 0.999 - 0.929 - 0.013 = 0.057 ms (0.054 / 0.119 / 0.085 by
    round), under the 0.10 ms kill line and consistent with sdtrace's
    `stop` hop (42/54 us). A1: issue2cmd 65 us + cmd2data 225 us per 4 KiB
    request = 0.29 ms, under the 1.0 ms family kill.
The auto_stop implementation (SDMMC_CMD_SEND_STOP for CMD18/25, request
ended at DATA_OVER in the sunxi form, ACD cleared beside the RXDR/TXDR
quirk) is preserved unbuilt in
artifacts/tracks/polled/patches/0064-dw-mmc-poll-autostop/ with its own
README; it is NOT in this driver. Recorded next to send_stop_abort().

