  poll_ns sweep at 4096 (04c): 500000 expired 5-10/300, 1500000 and
    3000000 1/300; p90 no longer tracks the budget. Default stays 1500000.
  Rule verdict: ctxt/req <= 1 in every poll arm (pass); p50 -0.33 ms on
    CPU0 (1.47 -> 1.14, six runs within 0.006), -0.17 on CPU1 (#374);
    p99 not above the 0 arm. The 4 KiB MIN moves only ~0.01 ms unpinned
    because the unpinned min already IS the CPU0 placement (1.00), where
    the fastest request has no wake to delete; the -0.20 ms the rule
    asked for (from the 1.17 baseline) is exactly the CPU1 placement's
    1.18 -> 0.97. 16 KiB min -0.15 to -0.27 on the 16384 arm.
  Knobs-0 no-op check on #374 and #375 (03-knobs0-sanity.sh): min
    1.007/1.005 and 0.998/0.997, ctxt/req 2.2-2.4, idle dw-mci IRQs over
    3 s = 0, no data error / did not quiesce.

  timedemo -mem 20, tyr-quake-x11, fresh boot per run, interleaved, 5 each
  (scripts/board/quake-timedemo.sh with PRE= setting the knob and POST=
  reading sdprobe/sdtrace; first run after the flash discarded):

    arm          fps (5 fresh boots)        mean  worst  majflt mean
    poll 16384   8.9  8.1  9.4  7.9  9.3    8.72  7.9    6,446
    poll 0       8.5  8.2  8.7  7.8  9.0    8.44  7.8    7,511
  Inside the -mem 20 boot band (7.8-9.4) - not claimed as an fps win;
  the guard (worst-of-5 not lower) passes. Hop ring since reset, run 5 of
  each (avg us): total 2526 vs 2871, po2bl 140 vs 244, bl2end 194 vs 242,
  indrv 1824 vs 2006. Under this load 19-23% of polled reads EXPIRE (a
  read queued behind a swap-out write outruns 1.5 ms): poll n/hit/expired
  6202/4769/1433 .. 8725/7072/1653 per run, avg spin 613-678 us, i.e.
  ~64 polls/s x 0.64 ms = ~4% of CPU0 spent spinning that the faulter used
  to sleep through. Net still positive on every judge above. A shorter
  budget under write load, or not polling while a write is in flight, is
  the obvious next arm (phase 2, item 5 is the same queue-behind-write
  tail from the other side).

COST: the spin is CPU on the issuing hart with BH disabled for the length
of the read (avg 270 us at 4 KiB; up to poll_ns). Under the timedemo see
the table; the guard was the worst-of-5 fps.

WRITE CHECK: scripts/board/sd-write-check.sh with poll_bytes=16384 -
kernel #375, poll_bytes=16384 set at runtime: 24 MB O_DIRECT
  write, drop_caches, sha256 MATCH (74052d2439af4c66), sdprobe busy n 13016
  waited 0, no MMC lines in dmesg (the three DMESG_ERRORS are the boot-time
  crypto self-test and regulatory.db, pre-existing). During the read-back
  16 of 26 polled reads expired - the card still programming the writes.

